```ts
function isMyType(value: unknown): value is MyType {
  return ...
}

const maybeMyTypeRef = ref(...)
if(refTypeGuard(isMyType, maybeMyTypeRef)) {
   // maybeMyTypeRef === Ref<MyType>
}
```

the type argument is `<T>` (any). 
the first argument is `TypeGuard<T>`. 
The second argument is `ref<unknown>`.

if you provide a type argument that conflicts with the TypeGuard it will not build
```ts
refTypeGuard<number>(isMyType, maybeMyTypeRef)
                    ~~~~~~~ <- error: type guard doesn't assert 'number'
```

